Package: tidymapr
Title: Tidy Mapping Verbs for Biodiversity and Spatial Ecology
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Jimmy", "Moses", , "jimmy.moses@pnguot.ac.pg", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Tidy, pipe-friendly mapping and geospatial verbs for
    biodiversity and spatial ecology. Turns site tables into 'sf' objects,
    joins raster values as columns, cleans occurrence records, computes
    geographic, elevational and environmental distances, draws
    publication-ready study-site, diversity and stem maps with 'ggplot2',
    reads and writes common vector and raster formats, downloads bioclim,
    elevation and administrative boundary layers, and fits simple species
    distribution models. Designed to work with 'tidydiversity' in the same
    way that 'dplyr' and 'ggplot2' do: every verb takes a data frame and
    returns a tibble or a 'ggplot', so the two packages share one workflow.
